// expect-error: allocated at line 21 but never freed
// BUG-966 (refactor L stage 2): a `defer` registered INSIDE a conditional block frees
// the handle only on the paths that ENTER that block. The fall-through path allocates
// and never frees.
//
// This compiled CLEAN before — measured on the pre-refactor compiler, and verified in
// the emitted C, where the false-branch block returns with no `_zer_slab_free_ptr` on
// that path. So it is a leak the analysis could not see, not merely a missing report.
//
// It was found while triaging tests/zer_gaps/audit2_defer_scan_nested.zer and was
// first recorded AS a gap; it then closed on the same day, as a second-order effect of
// tagging the ENDING block of a bare `orelse return` fallback (see the BUG-966 comment
// in lower_orelse_to_dest). The compile-time defer stack correctly pops the defer at
// the end of the block, so no fire is emitted at the outer return — right for
// emission, and exactly what used to leave the handle unaccounted for.

struct Task { u32 id; }
Slab(Task) heap;

u32 main() {
    *Task t = heap.alloc_ptr() orelse { return 1; };
    bool c = true;
    if (c) {
        defer heap.free_ptr(t);
        return t.id;
    }
    return 0;
}
